<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20960] FLR-ECRO: FIEMAP blocks on EC file with unavailable OST</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20960</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;ioctl(FS_IOC_FIEMAP)&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;filefrag&lt;/tt&gt;) on an EC file with a data stripe on an unavailable OST blocks until the OST returns.  See the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20212" title="FLR-ECRO: verify non-write RPCs do not block client " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20212"&gt;LU-20212&lt;/a&gt; test results.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;ptlrpc_queue_wait &amp;lt; osc_object_fiemap &amp;lt; cl_object_fiemap &amp;lt; fiemap_for_stripe &amp;lt; lov_object_fiemap &amp;lt; cl_object_fiemap &amp;lt; ll_do_fiemap
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The FIEMAP RPC to the unavailable OST could be sent no-delay and its extent returned with &lt;tt&gt;FIEMAP_EXTENT_UNKNOWN&lt;/tt&gt; (the data can be read, but its placement is not known), instead of waiting for the OST.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
